{"title":"Career roadmap · Event Executive","role":"Event Executive","summary":"An Event Executive supports the planning, coordination, execution, and post-event management of conferences, corporate events, exhibitions, seminars, weddings, cultural programmes, product launches, award functions, college events, and virtual/hybrid events.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career alignment"},{"type":"p","text":"An Event Executive supports the planning, coordination, execution, and post-event management of conferences, corporate events, exhibitions, seminars, weddings, cultural programmes, product launches, award functions, college events, and virtual/hybrid events."},{"type":"p","text":"A BA in Advertising, Public Relations, or Event Management provides a strong foundation in communication, audience engagement, promotions, event planning, public relations, vendor coordination, and marketing. To become employable, students should combine this with event operations, budgeting, project management, digital marketing, event technology, and practical event experience."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical Roles"],"rows":[[{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"Event Intern, Event Assistant, Event Coordinator"}],[{"text":"Early Career"},{"text":"Event Executive, Event Operations Executive, Event Marketing Executive"}],[{"text":"Mid Career"},{"text":"Senior Event Executive, Event Manager, Project Manager"}],[{"text":"Advanced"},{"text":"Senior Event Manager, Event Operations Manager, Account Manager"}],[{"text":"Leadership"},{"text":"Head of Events, Event Director, Experiential Marketing Head"}],[{"text":"Entrepreneurship"},{"text":"Event Agency Founder, Independent Event Consultant"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During the BA","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Communication + Event Fundamentals"},{"type":"h","t