udience Insights"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Future"},{"type":"flow","items":["AI Event Planning","Hybrid Events","Immersive Experiences","Event Technology"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Target Progression"},{"type":"h","text":"BA Advertising / PR / Event Management"},{"type":"h","text":"Event Intern / Event Assistant"},{"type":"h","text":"Event Executive"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Event Executive"},{"type":"h","text":"Event Manager"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Event Manager / Event Operations Manager"},{"type":"h","text":"Event Director / Head of Events"},{"type":"h","text":"Experiential Marketing Head / Event Agency Founder / Event Consultant"},{"type":"h","text":"Best overall strategy"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA","real event experience","event operations","digital marketing","budgeting","vendor management","project management","analytics","AI/event technology is the strongest combination."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"For this career, the student's portfolio should demonstrate actual events executed, not just certificates: event proposals, budgets, run-of-show documents, vendor comparisons, marketing campaigns, registration dashboards, event photographs/documentation, post-event reports, and measurable outcomes."}]}]}